---
description: TaskHub Backend Best Practices & Style Guide
globs: apps/api/**/*.cs
---

- Follow Single Responsibility Principle and use constructor-based Dependency Injection.
- All I/O-bound operations must be async/await.
- Use immutable DTOs/models where possible.
- Organize code by feature: Controllers, Core, Infrastructure, Services, Hubs.
- Use repository pattern for data access; abstract with interfaces.
- Use LINQ for queries, AsNoTracking for read-only, and manage schema via EF Core migrations.
- Use xUnit for TDD, with Arrange-Act-Assert structure and proper naming.
- Use Serilog for structured logging and implement global exception middleware.
- Validate DTOs with FluentValidation; return 400 on validation errors.
- Naming: PascalCase for classes/methods/properties, camelCase for locals, I-prefixed interfaces, _ for private fields.
- File names must match primary class.
- Use explicit namespace qualification for non-primitive types unless using statements are present.